From: WorkBuddy <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: apply BE7000 runtime radio count in htc

The Xiaomi BE7000 selects its 5 GHz radio mode at probe time through the
be7000_dual module parameter; 305-be7000-radio-mode.patch provides
ath12k_be7000_num_radios() for qmi.c and wmi.c. htc.c must use the same
value, otherwise the static DT property qcom,num-radios (=1) caps the WMI
endpoint count at one and MAC1 can never connect in tri-band mode.

This hunk is deliberately applied AFTER
908-ath12k-limit-wmi-endpoints-to-phy-capability.patch: that upstream patch
uses the original of_property_read_u32() lines as hunk context, so changing
them earlier (in 305) makes 908 fail with "Hunk #1 FAILED at 779".
Keeping the DT read intact until now lets 908 apply unchanged, while the
final code is identical to the original 305 design.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/htc.c
@@ -779,14 +779,14 @@ int ath12k_htc_init(struct ath12k_base *
 		break;
 	}
 
 	/* PHY capability is queried before firmware startup. A chip's maximum
 	 * radio count can exceed the PHYs enabled by its board firmware.
 	 */
 	if (ab->qmi.num_radios && ab->qmi.num_radios <= ab->hw_params->max_radios)
 		htc->wmi_ep_count = min_t(u8, htc->wmi_ep_count, ab->qmi.num_radios);
 
-	if (!of_property_read_u32(ab->dev->of_node, "qcom,num-radios",
-				  &num_radios) && num_radios) {
+	extern int ath12k_be7000_num_radios(struct ath12k_base *, u32 *);
+	if (!ath12k_be7000_num_radios(ab, &num_radios) && num_radios) {
 		num_radios = min_t(u32, num_radios, ab->hw_params->max_radios);
 		htc->wmi_ep_count = min_t(u8, htc->wmi_ep_count, num_radios);
 	}
